Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:51:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/24] gpu: write type-0 shader constant ranges in bulk

Some games (GRAW) upload their shader constants with type-0 packets
instead of SET_CONSTANT: about 200 registers per draw, over a million per
frame, each one going through the virtual WriteRegister and the backend's
per-register constant dirty check.

When a type-0 packet writes consecutive registers that all fall within
the shader constant range (float, fetch, bool and loop constants), hand
the whole range to WriteRegisterRangeFromRing, the same bulk path that
type-3 SET_CONSTANT packets use: one copy and one dirty check in the
backend's WriteRegistersFromMem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/command_processor.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
index 9406692..9428a78 100644
--- a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
@@ -718,6 +718,14 @@ bool CommandProcessor::ExecutePacketType0(memory::RingBuffer* reader, uint32_t p
 
   uint32_t base_index = (packet & 0x7FFF);
   uint32_t write_one_reg = (packet >> 15) & 0x1;
+  // Perf: GRAW also writes its shader constants with type-0 packets (~200 registers per draw,
+  // 1.4M per frame); hand whole constant ranges to the bulk path (one copy + one dirty check in the
+  // backend's WriteRegistersFromMem) instead of one virtual WriteRegister per dword.
+  if (!write_one_reg && base_index >= XE_GPU_REG_SHADER_CONSTANT_000_X &&
+      base_index + count - 1 <= XE_GPU_REG_SHADER_CONSTANT_LOOP_31) {
+    WriteRegisterRangeFromRing(reader, base_index, count);
+    return true;
+  }
   volatile uint32_t* reg_values = register_file_->values;  // volatile for the WAIT_REG_MEM loop
   for (uint32_t m = 0; m < count; m++) {
     uint32_t reg_data = reader->ReadAndSwap<uint32_t>();
